0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Travis Mitchell Snap Shot Wide Right","type":{"id":"507","text":"Missed","abbreviation":"shot-missed"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:14"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"25"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5173614","displayName":"Travis Mitchell","shortName":"T. Mitchell"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"4576894","displayName":"Arturs Silovs","shortName":"A. Silovs"}}]},{"id":"401892679000000680","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Beckett Sennecke Tip-In Wide Left","type":{"id":"507","text":"Missed","abbreviation":"shot-missed"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:18"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"25"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5216858","displayName":"Beckett Sennecke","shortName":"B. Sennecke"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"4576894","displayName":"Arturs Silovs","shortName":"A. Silovs"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1842","fullName":"Honda Center","address":{"city":"Anaheim","state":"CA","zipCode":"92899","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1842.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17174,"officials":[{"fullName":"Scott Cherrey","displayName":"Scott Cherrey","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Cody Beach","displayName":"Cody Beach","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Chris Rooney","displayName":"Chris Rooney","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Joe Mahon","displayName":"Joe Mahon","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Cutter Gauthier gets his 3rd hat trick in November, propelling the prolific Ducks past Penguins 5-2","description":"— Cutter Gauthier continued his scoring rampage with his third hat trick in eight days, and captain Mikael Granlund had a goal and three assists in the Anaheim Ducks' fifth consecutive victory, 5-2 over the Pittsburgh Penguins on Sunday night.","story":"ANAHEIM, Calif. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080145/cutter-gauthier\">Cutter Gauthier</a> continued his scoring rampage with his third hat trick in eight days, and captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5831/mikael-granlund\">Mikael Granlund</a> had a goal and three assists in the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ana/anaheim-ducks\">Anaheim Ducks</a>' fifth consecutive victory, 5-2 over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/pit/pittsburgh-penguins\">Pittsburgh Penguins</a> on Sunday night.\n\n\r\n              Gauthier’s empty-net goal in the final minute gave him three goals and an assist for the Ducks, who became the first team since the 1988-89 <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/la/los-angeles-kings\">Los Angeles Kings</a> to score at least five goals in eight consecutive games.\n\n\r\n              Gauthier extended his goals streak to six games and his points streak to a career best-tying eight games with his fourth multi-goal performance during this electric sequence, including three of his four career hat tricks. He has scored eight of his 13 goals in this six-game stretch on power plays.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565262/jackson-lacombe\">Jackson LaCombe</a> had three assists and tied a Ducks record with an assist in his 10th consecutive game. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3026526/laurent-brossoit\">Laurent Brossoit</a> made 32 saves for his fourth victory in four starts in Anaheim’s net.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3539/kris-letang\">Kris Letang</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562629/rickard-rakell\">Rickard Rakell</a> scored 6-on-4 power-play goals in the third period after Pittsburgh had fallen behind 4-0. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3124/evgeni-malkin\">Evgeni Malkin</a> had two assists and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4576894/arturs-silovs\">Arturs Silovs</a> stopped 20 shots for the Penguins, who snapped a four-game skid <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/penguins-kings-score-sidney-crosby-ec0984f845a8eaedab24988d2658307a\">Saturday night at Los Angeles</a> in the opener of their California trip.\n\n\r\n              Granlund scored from the slot in the first period right as a power play ended, extending his scoring streak to six games.\n\n\r\n              After Pittsburgh failed to score during nearly 4 1/2 straight minutes of power-play time early in the second, Gauthier beat Silovs with a beautiful no-look shot for his first goal. Gauthier scored again less than three minutes later with a quick wrist shot.\n\n\r\n              Luneau ripped a power-play goal early in the third and extended his point streak to eight games, justifying the faith shown when the Ducks signed the defenseman <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/tristan-luneau-anaheim-ducks-22659b53f60d30a83f715a98bf9596e7\">to a $43.2 million extension</a> last month before his first full NHL season.\n\n\r\n              Pittsburgh avoided the shutout on Letang's 6-on-4 score with 11:55 to play, the first goal of his 21st NHL season.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Penguins: At San Jose on Wednesday night.\n\n\r\n              Ducks: Host Nashville on Wednesday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-09T03:51:34Z"}}